<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassandrēa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-īa</span></b> , ae, f.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in
				Macedonia</i>, <i>upon the peninsula Pallene</i>,
				<i>previously called Potidœa</i>, <i>but rebuilt by Cassander</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
				8, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">44, 11,
				1</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10,
				17, § 36</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassandrenses</span></b> ,
			ium, m., <i>the inhabitants
				of Cassandrea</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 44, 10, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 50,
				15, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassandreus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ei,
				m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κασσανδρεύς</span>,
				<i>of Cassandrea</i>, <i>a surname of
				the tyrant</i> Apollodorus, <i>who reigned
			there</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 2, 9, 43</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>